  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q31-34-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Write the following in the form $Q(x)+\\dfrac{R(x)}{D(x)}$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q31-34-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^3+2x-1}{x+3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2-3x+11-\\dfrac{34}{x+3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x^3+0x^2+2x-1)-x^2(x+3)&=-3x^2+2x-1\\\\(-3x^2+2x-1)-(-3x)(x+3)&=11x-1\\\\(11x-1)-11(x+3)&=-34\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $Q(x)=x^2-3x+11$ and $R(x)=-34$.\n\n$$\\frac{x^3+2x-1}{x+3}=x^2-3x+11-\\frac{34}{x+3}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q31-34-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1+x+x^2+x^3}{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2+2x+3+\\dfrac4{x-1}$",
          "worked": "Arrange the numerator in descending powers.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^3+x^2+x+1)-x^2(x-1)&=2x^2+x+1\\\\(2x^2+x+1)-2x(x-1)&=3x+1\\\\(3x+1)-3(x-1)&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $Q(x)=x^2+2x+3$ and $R(x)=4$.\n\n$$\\frac{1+x+x^2+x^3}{x-1}=x^2+2x+3+\\frac4{x-1}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q31-34-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^3+3x^2+4x-5}{x^2+2x+4}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x+1-\\dfrac{2x+9}{x^2+2x+4}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x^3+3x^2+4x-5)-x(x^2+2x+4)&=x^2-5\\\\(x^2+0x-5)-(x^2+2x+4)&=-2x-9\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $Q(x)=x+1$ and $R(x)=-2x-9$.\n\n$$\\frac{x^3+3x^2+4x-5}{x^2+2x+4}=x+1-\\frac{2x+9}{x^2+2x+4}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q31-34-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^4-x+1}{x^2+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2-1-\\dfrac{x-2}{x^2+1}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x^4+0x^3+0x^2-x+1)-x^2(x^2+1)&=-x^2-x+1\\\\(-x^2-x+1)-(-1)(x^2+1)&=-x+2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $Q(x)=x^2-1$ and $R(x)=-x+2$.\n\n$$\\frac{x^4-x+1}{x^2+1}=x^2-1-\\frac{x-2}{x^2+1}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
